[section:MutableEndpointSequence Mutable endpoint sequence requirements]

A ['mutable endpoint sequence] is a range of endpoints into which an operation,
such as the `receive_from_multiple` operation of a datagram socket, writes the
source endpoint of each received datagram.

A type `X` meets the `MutableEndpointSequence` requirements if it satisfies the
requirements of `Destructible` (C++Std [destructible]) and `CopyConstructible`
(C++Std [copyconstructible]), and
[link asio.reference.is_shallow_mutable_sequence
`is_shallow_mutable_sequence<X>::value`] is `true`, as well as the additional
requirements listed below.

In the table below, `x` denotes a value of type `X`, or of type `R` if `X` is
`std::reference_wrapper<R>`, `i` denotes an iterator in the range
[half_open_range `x.begin()`,`x.end()`], and `e` denotes `*i`, or `(*i).get()`
if `*i` is a `std::reference_wrapper`.

[table MutableEndpointSequence requirements
  [[expression] [return type] [assertion/note[br]pre/post-condition]]
  [
    [`x.begin()`[br]
     `x.end()`]
    [A type meeting the requirements for forward iterators
     (C++Std \[forward.iterators\]).]
    [[half_open_range `x.begin()`,`x.end()`] is a valid range. The range
     may be traversed more than once.]
  ]
  [
    [`e`]
    [A type satisfying the [link asio.reference.Endpoint `Endpoint`]
     requirements.]
    [`e` must be modifiable. On completion, holds the source endpoint of the
     corresponding datagram.]
  ]
]

[endsect]
